{{- /* The reply to a replan in review maul refused: what it would have
replaced cannot be planned again. The pull requests are maul's own, linked on
purpose. */ -}}
{{ .Marker }}
{{ if eq .Reason "merged" -}}
{{ .Asked }} does nothing once a pull request of this intent has merged: what merged is already on its repository's default branch, and a new plan cannot replace it. Review the rest as it is, or {{ code "/maul cancel" }} and open a new issue.
{{- with .Merged }}

**Merged:**
{{ range . }}
- [{{ .Ref }}]({{ .URL }})
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- else if eq .Reason "all-merged" -}}
{{ .Asked }} does nothing: every pull request of this intent merged before maul could close it for the new plan, so the intent is complete and nothing is planned again. Open a new issue for what is still to change.
{{- with .Merged }}

**Merged:**
{{ range . }}
- [{{ .Ref }}]({{ .URL }})
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- else if eq .Reason "cost" -}}
{{ .Asked }} does nothing while this intent is at its cost ceiling: it has spent {{ code .Spent }} of the project's {{ code .Ceiling }}, and a new plan would be stopped by the same ceiling before it could be written. Raise {{ code "limits.maxCostMicroUSD" }}, then replan.
{{- else -}}
{{ .Asked }} does nothing: this intent has no plan revision left. {{ code "/maul cancel" }} and open a new issue.
{{- end }}
